---
// The techniques index (#416 (engine and player)): one line per technique,
// a link for each page that exists (src/lib/techniques.mjs).
import Doc from "../../layouts/Doc.astro";
import { url } from "../../nav";
import { TECHNIQUES } from "../../lib/techniques.mjs";
---
<Doc
  title="Techniques"
  kicker="techniques"
  section="techniques/"
  description="Each page shows one technique of moonpool in a live run: the problem, the technique, the run, the code."
>
  <ol class="index-list">
    {TECHNIQUES.map((t) => (
      <li>
        {t.path ? <a class="n" href={url(t.path)}>{t.name}</a> : <span class="n">{t.name} <span class="chip-status">to come</span></span>}
        <span class="desc">{t.line}</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>
  <p>Each live run is a real moonpool run, compiled to wasm, in your browser. The same small system runs on each
    page: three servers keep one value on disk, and a client writes it and reads it back.
    The <a href={url("guide/")}>Guide</a> explains each technique in full.</p>
</Doc>
